---
title: Invoices
---
<script>
  // The documents — and the one list in this app whose columns, headers,
  // filters and cells all come out of `db/schema.lite`.
  //
  // Nothing on this screen edits anything, and that is the model rather than a
  // decision here: `Invoice` is `@@gate("1.8.8.8")` and every money column on
  // it is `@system @immutable`, so the writable set is empty and there is no
  // form to generate (`FJS-D162`). What a person may do to an invoice is
  // settle it or void it, and both are named moves on its own screen. A table
  // over a model nobody can write is the shape `columns()` is FOR: a form
  // shows what is writable and there is none, a table shows what is readable
  // and identifying and that is the whole model.
  //
  // ─── What is derived, and what is still this app's ──────────────────────
  //
  // Derived: which columns, their headers, which of them a header may sort by,
  // what each filter ASKS, and how every value renders. No list of fields
  // exists in this file — `only:` below names six of them and that is an
  // ORDER, not a set of labels or types.
  //
  // This app's, and unable to be anything else:
  //
  //   overdue   `dueAt` against the clock. Not a status and must not be — it
  //             is true from one moment onward with nothing writing a row, so
  //             a column for it would be a value that goes stale while nobody
  //             is looking.
  //   the tone  whether `void` is bad news. No attribute decides that
  //             (`web/src/status-tone.js`).
  //   the money the reader's chosen currency, which the schema is right not to
  //             carry (`web/src/displays.js`).
  //
  // The last two reach the cells as REGISTRATIONS rather than as branches
  // here, which is what keeps this table the same table the generator writes.
  import { invoices } from '@/resources/Invoice.mesa'
  import { session } from '@/session.js'
  import { prefs } from '@/prefs.js'

  import Alert         from '@frontierjs/ui/components/feedback/Alert.mesa'
  import Button        from '@frontierjs/ui/components/forms/Button.mesa'
  import Cell          from '@frontierjs/ui/components/display/Cell.mesa'
  import FilterBar     from '@frontierjs/ui/components/display/FilterBar.mesa'
  import Pill          from '@frontierjs/ui/components/display/Pill.mesa'
  import SectionHeader from '@frontierjs/ui/components/display/SectionHeader.mesa'
  import Table         from '@frontierjs/ui/components/display/Table.mesa'

  // ── Which columns ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // The six, and the order, are `resources/Invoice.mesa`'s: a ledger is what a
  // list of invoices IS, wherever one is listed. `omitted` is what keeps that
  // from being a silent choice — every column this table does NOT show is named
  // below with the reason. Basecamp's deployments table takes the ranking
  // unaided; between the two, both halves of `columns()` have a caller.
  const { columns: cols, omitted } = invoices.columns()

  // A header offers a sort only where the SCHEMA takes one: `x-sortable` is
  // emitted as an exception, so absent means yes and a string says why not.
  const columns = [
    ...cols,
    { name: '_open', label: '' },
  ]

  // `Invoice` declares no `@@fts`, so `search` comes back refused WITH the
  // reason and no box is drawn — a search box that 400s on every word is worse
  // than none.
  const { filters, search } = invoices.filters()

  $: (session.level, prefs.dense, prefs.currency)

  // ── The URL is the state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // `list()` reads `page.query` and `page.directives`, loads, re-runs on a
  // navigation, and navigates on `apply` and `sort` — so a filtered, sorted
  // list is a LINK. The resource file's `-issuedAt` sits under the URL's
  // directives, so `?$orderBy=number` wins, and the header reads the same
  // directives the load sends, default included, or a sorted list arrives with
  // no column marked.
  const list = invoices.list()

  // Overdue is not a status. It is `dueAt` against the clock, so it is true
  // from one moment onward with nothing writing a row.
  const overdue = (inv) => inv.status === 'issued' && new Date(inv.dueAt) < new Date()
</script>

<SectionHeader title="Invoices" level={1}>
  {#snippet action()}
    <div class="cluster">
      <a class="navlink" href="/plans/">Plans</a>
      <a class="navlink" href="/subscriptions/">Subscriptions</a>
    </div>
  {/snippet}
</SectionHeader>

{#if list.error}<Alert tone="danger" id="i-error">{list.error.message}</Alert>{/if}

<FilterBar id="i-filters" {filters} {search} value={list.query}
            directives={list.directives} onchange={list.apply} />

<Table {columns} rows={list.rows} orderBy={list.directives.orderBy} onsort={list.sort}
       striped hover compact={prefs.dense} emptyText="No invoice matches that.">
  {#snippet row(inv)}
    <tr data-invoice={inv.id} data-number={inv.number}>
      {#each cols as c}
        <td data-col={c.name} data-value={inv[c.name]}>
          <Cell value={inv[c.name]} column={c} record={inv} />
          <!-- The one thing beside a derived cell, and the reason it is beside
               rather than inside: no schema can answer it. -->
          {#if c.name === 'status' && overdue(inv)}
            <Pill tone="danger" data-overdue="true">overdue</Pill>
          {/if}
        </td>
      {/each}
      <td><Button variant="ghost" href={'/invoices/' + inv.id + '/'} data-open>Open</Button></td>
    </tr>
  {/snippet}
</Table>

{#if list.hasMore}
  <Button variant="ghost" id="i-more" onclick={list.more}>Load more</Button>
{/if}

<Alert tone="info" id="i-derived">
  Every header, every filter and every cell above came out of
  <code>db/schema.lite</code>. <code>status</code> is an enum, so it filters by
  membership; <code>total</code> is <code>@money</code>, so it filters by range
  and renders as money rather than as the integer number of cents it is stored
  as; <code>customerId</code> is a foreign key, so it filters by the rows it
  points at. No list of fields or types exists in the page.
</Alert>

<Alert tone="muted" id="i-nosearch">
  <strong>There is no search box</strong>, and that is an answer rather than an
  omission: <code>Invoice</code> declares no <code>@@fts</code>, so the Data
  boundary refuses <code>$search</code> by name and the bar says
  <em>{search.reason}</em>. <code>Product</code> is the model here that does
  declare one.
</Alert>

{#if omitted.length}
  <p class="text-sm text-muted" id="i-omitted">
    Not shown: {omitted.map(o => o.name).join(', ')} — each with a reason, so a
    column added to the schema that does not appear here is answerable without
    reading the page.
  </p>
{/if}

<Alert tone="muted">
  <strong>overdue</strong> is not a status. It is <code>dueAt</code> against the
  clock — true from one moment onward with nothing writing a row — which is also
  the only thing dunning counts: <em>how long has this been unpaid</em> is
  <code>now − dueAt</code> on the oldest unpaid invoice, so no counter is kept
  anywhere and no counter can disagree with the rows.
</Alert>
